abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. For two-qubit states with steering-ellipsoid centre length c and Bob Bloch length r, the CHSH bound beta^2/4 <= 1 + (1 - r^2)(1 - 2c) and its attaining value are prior work (the Omega Institute's public record of 14 October 2026 for Milne et al.'s Conjecture 1; Zhang et al. 2020); no priority is claimed for them. For 0 < c < 1 the extremizers form one local-unitary class, a filtered maximally obese state with |b|^2 = b_z. Trace-norm rigidity holds near equality, with a uniform exponent 1/4 that is optimal. Exact fixed-radius CHSH envelopes are given for all axial and all centred steering ellipsoids, with an exact CHSH-breaking criterion for axial qubit channels, and a printed optimizing direction in Zhang et al. is corrected. Lean 4 checks an actual density matrix with exact CHSH supremum 2 sqrt(1 + (1 - 2c)(1 - r^2)) for every admissible (c, r), further witnesses and the axial spectral optimization. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
